(LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE). The project used to live at
github.com/bherbruck/solidcraft, which redirects to the address above.

Three skills are adapted from the skills of earthtojake/text-to-cad
(https://github.com/earthtojake/text-to-cad, commit
a7cf2c470e345d6b6a2fe373a73e0420ff64ad2a, MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2026
Thompson Labs LLC): solidcraft-dfm-review (from `dfm` and `sendcutsend`),
solidcraft-step-parts (from `step-parts`) and solidcraft-engineering-drawing
(from `engineering-drawing`). They are rewritten for SolidCraft and their helper
scripts are original. The table in skills/solidcraft-3d-print-dfm/references/
process-limits.md is taken from its `dfam-check` skill. Those skills' MIT
licence permits this use; the licence text is in the text-to-cad repository.
solidcraft-dfm-review reads public data files published by
SendCutSend, and solidcraft-step-parts reads the public step.parts catalog;
neither service is affiliated with this repository.

Three further skills take ideas from other MIT-licensed projects and are rewritten
for SolidCraft, with no text copied: solidcraft-requirements-and-sanity and
solidcraft-delivery-gate from the process gates of capwitf/mechanical-cad-skills
(https://github.com/capwitf/mechanical-cad-skills), and solidcraft-hole-fastener-rules
from the hole, fastener and gear guidance of wzyn20051216/solidworks-automation-skill
(https://github.com/wzyn20051216/solidworks-automation-skill). The reference values in
the latter are standard figures (ISO 273 clearance holes, coarse tap drills, gear
formulas) and starting values the repository author asks readers to confirm. Neither
project is affiliated with this repository.

All other skills in `skills/` are original to this repository. They mention
public tutorials and public speed-modeling challenges only to record
lessons learned. They contain no drawings, videos or solution files from
those sources, and the authors of those works are not affiliated with this
repository.

The notes in `skills/solidcraft-sheet-metal-flatpack/references/` summarise a
public article (Hackaday, "The Art And Science Of Bending Sheet Metal") and
measurements read from the public assembly video of the das_POD CD-ROM Player 01.
They are the repository's own summaries and estimates. They are not endorsed by,
and contain no files from, the authors or makers of those works.

The note in `skills/solidcraft-sheet-metal/references/` summarises two public tutorial
videos by the YouTube channel Elite Engineers (https://www.youtube.com/@elite_engineers), read from frames, with the repository's
own rebuild results. It contains no files from the author, who is not affiliated with
this repository.

The models in `examples/sheet-metal-tutorials/` are the repository author's own rebuilds of
those tutorials from frames, not the author's files.

The models in `examples/cdrom-player-flatpack/` are approximate teaching reconstructions
by the repository author. They are not manufacturing files, and the design of the
product they depict remains the maker's.

